  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "Acceptance tests will be implemented using JUnit 5 and Cucumber for BDD-style scenarios.",
    "Testcontainers will be used for external dependencies (e.g., Splunk, Kafka, Spark) to ensure isolated and reproducible tests.",
    "Acceptance tests will be placed in a separate source set (e.g., `src/acceptanceTest`) to allow separate execution in CI.",
    "The CI pipeline will be extended with a dedicated acceptance test stage that runs after integration tests.",
    "Each module's acceptance tests will cover at least the happy path, configuration variations, and error handling."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "The project uses Gradle as the build tool.",
    "The CI system is GitHub Actions (or similar) and we have permission to modify the pipeline.",
    "The modules (null, rich_gauge, router, shell, splunk, throughput-sampler, spark-app, timestampfile) are already implemented and functional; we are only adding acceptance tests.",
    "The necessary external systems (Splunk, Spark, etc.) are available as Docker images for Testcontainers.",
    "The team has experience with the testing frameworks and CI configuration.",
    "Each module's acceptance test effort is similar, with an average of 16 hours per module (including analysis, implementation, debugging, CI integration, and review).",
    "Common infrastructure setup (test framework, base classes, CI configuration) is required once and shared across all modules."
  ],
